<title>CROATIA: Croatian PM to discuss peace, economy in Kuwait.</title>
<headline>Croatian PM to discuss peace, economy in Kuwait.</headline>
<dateline>ZAGREB 1997-03-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>Croatian Prime Minister Zlatko Matesa left on Friday on a three-day visit to Kuwait where he will discuss bilateral economic cooperation and the peace process in the Balkans, state news agency HINA reported.</p>
<p>Matesa recently returned from a week-long visit to Malaysia aimed at boosting trade and wooing Malaysian investments in the former Yugoslav republic.</p>
<p>&quot;We are not entirely satisfied with our economic cooperation with Kuwait but there are great potentials,&quot; Matesa told the agency before departing.</p>
<p>&quot;I think some investments and business Croatia could do in Kuwait may be agreed during my visit,&quot; he said.</p>
</text>
